---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
import '~/styles/legal.css';

export const prerender = true;

const UPDATED = '5 August 2026';
const DISCORD = 'https://discord.com/invite/2sYR5YdRpH';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What PoGo TXK collects, why, and how to have it deleted. A volunteer-run community site for Pokémon GO players in Texarkana."
>
  <article class="legal">
    <p class="legal-eyebrow">PoGo TXK</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated {UPDATED}</p>

    <div class="legal-summary">
      <p><strong>The short version.</strong></p>
      <p>
        You can browse the whole site without an account. If you sign in, we store your Discord
        username, avatar and account ID so we know who you are — and nothing else unless you
        type it in yourself.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not sell your data, we do not run advertising, and we do not track you across
        other websites. Ask any ambassador on Discord and we will delete your account.
      </p>
    </div>

    <nav class="legal-toc" aria-label="Contents">
      <p>Contents</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#who">Who we are</a></li>
        <li><a href="#collect">What we collect</a></li>
        <li><a href="#why">Why we collect it</a></li>
        <li><a href="#discord">Signing in with Discord</a></li>
        <li><a href="#third-parties">Third parties</a></li>
        <li><a href="#retention">How long we keep it</a></li>
        <li><a href="#rights">Your choices</a></li>
        <li><a href="#children">Children</a></li>
        <li><a href="#security">Security</a></li>
        <li><a href="#changes">Changes</a></li>
        <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="who">1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      PoGo TXK is a volunteer-run community site for Pokémon GO players in Texarkana, Texas and
      Arkansas. It is not a company, and nobody is paid to run it. This policy covers the
      website and any companion app we publish under the same name.
    </p>

    <h2 id="collect">2. What we collect</h2>

    <h3>If you never sign in</h3>
    <p>
      Nothing that identifies you. We do not use analytics, advertising trackers, or
      cookies for visitors who are not signed in. Our hosting provider processes your IP
      address to serve the page, as any web host must.
    </p>

    <h3>If you sign in with Discord</h3>
    <p>We store the following in our database:</p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Data</th><th>Where it comes from</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Discord account ID</td><td>Discord, when you authorise sign-in</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Discord username and display name</td><td>Discord</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Discord avatar reference</td><td>Discord</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Whether you are in our Discord server, and which of our roles you hold</td><td>Discord</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Your site role (guest, member, ambassador, admin)</td><td>Worked out from the above</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Team, trainer name, trainer level, trainer code</td><td>Only if you enter them yourself. All optional.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>When you last signed in</td><td>Recorded automatically</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>We also keep, for as long as your session or the record lasts:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>A session record.</strong> Your sign-in cookie holds a random token. We store
        only a one-way hash of it, never the token itself, alongside its expiry and a
        short hash of your browser's user-agent string used to spot session hijacking.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A change log.</strong> If you are an ambassador or admin, edits you make to
        locations, posts and meetups are recorded with your account ID, so the community can
        see who changed what.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Things you post.</strong> Photos you upload, locations you submit, reports you
        file, and meetup or raid activity you take part in.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      <strong>We never receive your Discord password, email address, or direct messages.</strong>
      Discord does not give them to us and we do not ask for them.
    </p>

    <h2 id="why">3. Why we collect it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>To know who you are</strong> — so you stay signed in and see the right things.</li>
      <li><strong>To decide what you can do</strong> — editing the map is limited to ambassadors and admins.</li>
      <li><strong>To confirm you are part of the community</strong> — membership of our Discord server is the check.</li>
      <li><strong>To keep the site honest</strong> — the change log lets us undo mistakes and see who made them.</li>
      <li><strong>To run community features</strong> — meetups, raid coordination, and the photo gallery.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not profile you, sell or rent your data, share it with advertisers, or use it to
      train machine learning models.
    </p>

    <h2 id="discord">4. Signing in with Discord</h2>
    <p>
      We use Discord as our only sign-in method. When you authorise it, we request two
      permissions:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>identify</code> — your account ID, username and avatar. Not your email.</li>
      <li>
        <code>guilds.members.read</code> — whether you are in the PoGo TXK Discord server and
        which roles you hold there. It does not grant access to your messages or to any other
        server you are in.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You can revoke this at any time from Discord under <em>User Settings → Authorized Apps</em>.
      Revoking stops future sign-ins; to have the data already stored removed, see{' '}
      <a href="#rights">Your choices</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      What Discord itself does with your data is governed by{' '}
      <a href="https://discord.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Discord's privacy policy</a>,
      not this one.
    </p>

    <h2 id="third-parties">5. Third parties</h2>
    <p>
      We keep these to a minimum, but some are unavoidable for a map site. Where a third party
      serves content directly to your browser, that party necessarily sees your IP address.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Who</th><th>What for</th><th>What they see</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Cloudflare</td>
          <td>Hosting, database, image storage</td>
          <td>Your IP address and requests, as our hosting provider</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Discord</td>
          <td>Sign-in</td>
          <td>That you signed in to this site</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>OpenStreetMap and CARTO</td>
          <td>Map tiles</td>
          <td>Your IP address, and which map tiles you loaded</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Leek Duck</td>
          <td>Raid boss and event artwork</td>
          <td>Your IP address when those images load</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Google or Apple Maps</td>
          <td>Only if you tap "Directions"</td>
          <td>Nothing unless you tap it — it is an ordinary outbound link</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 id="retention">6. How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your account:</strong> until you ask us to delete it.</li>
      <li><strong>Sessions:</strong> two weeks from last use, then removed automatically.</li>
      <li><strong>Raid and meetup activity:</strong> raid flares expire within hours; attendance records persist as community history.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Change log:</strong> kept indefinitely, because its purpose is an accurate record
        of who edited what. If you delete your account, entries remain but are no longer linked
        to you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Photos:</strong> kept until removed by an ambassador. Photos of the community at
        public events may remain in the gallery with their original credit.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="rights">7. Your choices</h2>
    <p>Ask any ambassador on our <a href={DISCORD} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Discord server</a> to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>See what we hold about you</li>
      <li>Correct anything wrong</li>
      <li>Delete your account and personal data</li>
      <li>Remove a specific photo you are in</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We will action it within a reasonable time — usually a few days, since this is run by
      volunteers. You do not need to give a reason.
    </p>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live you may have additional rights under laws such as the GDPR or
      the CCPA. We aim to honour requests of that kind regardless of where you are, because the
      simplest policy is to just do it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="children">8. Children</h2>
    <p>
      Discord requires users to be at least 13, and older in some countries. Because signing in
      requires a Discord account, the same applies here. We do not knowingly collect data from
      anyone below that age. If you believe a child's data is stored here, tell an ambassador
      and we will remove it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="security">9. Security</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served over HTTPS. Sign-in tokens are stored only as one-way hashes, so a
      copy of our database could not be used to sign in as you. Access to the admin console is
      limited to ambassadors and admins.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are volunteers, not a security team. We will not pretend the site is impenetrable — do
      not store anything here you would be upset to see made public. If you find a
      vulnerability, please report it privately on Discord rather than publicly.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">10. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If we change this policy materially we will announce it in the Discord server and update
      the date at the top. Continuing to use the site after a change means you accept it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">11. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      The fastest way to reach us is the{' '}
      <a href={DISCORD} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">PoGo TXK Discord server</a> —
      message any ambassador or admin.
    </p>

    <p class="legal-note">
      PoGo TXK is a fan community and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by
      Niantic, Nintendo, Creatures Inc., GAME FREAK, or The Pokémon Company. Pokémon and
      Pokémon character names are trademarks of Nintendo. This policy covers only data handled
      by this site — playing Pokémon GO itself is governed by Niantic's own privacy policy.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
